Root cause:
The bug was caused by using an incorrect pointer when setting a 2MB page table entry (PTE) in the `radix__map_kernel_page()` function. Specifically, the code was incorrectly casting the `pudp` pointer instead of using the correct `pmdp` pointer to obtain the appropriate PTE. This led to potential memory management issues, as the wrong address could be referenced, resulting in incorrect mapping of kernel pages. The fix involved replacing the cast with a proper function call (`pmdp_ptep()`) to ensure the correct pointer was used.
